Project "tellme_session_history" {
  database_type: "JSON Lines (append-only local file)"
  Note: '''
  The persisted session-history model for tellme (rounds 007–008, 014). One conversation is a sequence of
  completed turns, stored as append-only JSON Lines under the per-mode session workspace
  ($TELL_ME_HOME/output/<mode>/). The active file is `history.jsonl`; `--new` moves its entries into
  `history.archive.jsonl`. The store is read wholesale on resume and written one line per completed turn.
  Round 008 widens a completed turn to also carry the tool activity it performed (the agent tool loop).
  Round 014 adds an optional, provider-agnostic `signature` to each tool step (the opaque token the model
  emitted for that call — for example the Gemini `thoughtSignature`), persisted only when the provider
  supplies one and omitted when empty, so a resumed session replays the step faithfully. The record is
  `{prompt, answer, steps:[{tool, arguments, result, signature?}]}`.
  It is not a relational database — this DBML pins the record shape and lifecycle so the CLI contract,
  the interface feature truth, and the implementation share a single model.
  '''
}

Enum history_location {
  active
  archived
}

Table history_entry {
  location history_location
  position int
  prompt text
  answer text

  indexes {
    (location, position) [pk]
  }

  Note: 'One completed exchange — the operator prompt and the provider answer — persisted as a single JSON line. Entries are append-only and ordered: within a file, `position` is the 1-based line ordinal (the record identity, since no ID or timestamp is stored) and the row order is the conversation order. `location` is `active` in `history.jsonl` and `archived` in `history.archive.jsonl`; `--new` moves every active entry to `archived` (entries from successive archived conversations append in order). An interrupted turn is never written, so no partial entry exists. Round 008: the entry ALSO embeds its ordered tool steps (see `history_step`), each optionally carrying a provider `signature` (round 014); `-l N` still surfaces only `prompt` and `answer`.'
}

Table history_step {
  location history_location
  position int
  step int
  tool varchar
  arguments text
  result text
  signature varchar

  indexes {
    (location, position, step) [pk]
  }

  Note: 'One tool execution performed during a completed turn (round 008 agent tool loop), embedded in the turn line as an element of its ordered steps array. `step` is the 1-based ordinal within the turn (which tool ran first, second, …); `tool` is the tool name (for example "list_files" or "read_files"); `arguments` is the model arguments (JSON-encoded) and `result` is the tool result or error, size-bounded (for example a file read capped at 1 MiB). Round 014 adds `signature`: the opaque, provider-agnostic token the provider emitted for this tool call (for example the Gemini 3 `thoughtSignature`), persisted only when the provider supplies one and omitted when empty (so a signature-less step serialises byte-identically to the round-008 shape). Read back and replayed VERBATIM into the conversation on resume, so a tool-using Gemini session replays the call faithfully; tellme never interprets, transforms, or expires it. Replayed as part of the synthesised tool call (no per-step id is stored — the adapter synthesises a deterministic tool-call id, `call_step_<step>`, when replaying); never surfaced by `-l`. A turn that made no tool calls has no `history_step` rows.'
}

Ref: history_step.(location, position) > history_entry.(location, position)
